# Claude Drive — one saw, nothing stacked (the Bocuma lesson: the voice
# is the envelope and the filter, not the mix). Ladder drive and tape
# drive pinned as asked, but no squelch: a modest filter-envelope bloom
# that decays over a couple of seconds, moderate resonance, strong key
# tracking, cutoff in the vowel range. Light triangle vibrato and a short
# auto glide keep held lines alive without an LFO sweep.
